From db525c8b9a5b8709d54a57b325252dce8df7dd3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mingcong Bai <jeffbai@aosc.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:39:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 471/471] AOSCOS: tools: iio: Check for __FLT16_MAX__ with SSE2
 availability on x86/x86-64
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When building the tools on i486/i586/i686 without SSE2, the build fails
with the following error:

  iio_generic_buffer.c:141:17: error: invalid conversion from type ‘_Float16’ without option ‘-msse2’
    141 |                 printf("%05f ", ((float)converter.f + info->offset) * info->scale);
        |                 ^~~~~~

Add a guard for x86 and x86-64, where `__FLT16_MAX__' is only considered
available if `__SSE2__' was defined (via -msse2, or implicitly via other
flags to the same effect).

A patch was submitted earlier to the list but no revision was made - this is another attempt at fixing this bug.

Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Fixes: cdd445d4b2a9 ("iio: tools: Add support for floating-point types in buffer scan elements")
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260918161305.1161852-1-iv@altlinux.org/
Suggested-by: Icenowy Zheng <zhengxingda@iscas.ac.cn>
Signed-off-by: Mingcong Bai <jeffbai@aosc.io>
---
 tools/iio/iio_generic_buffer.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/iio/iio_generic_buffer.c b/tools/iio/iio_generic_buffer.c
index 000193612aad2..df7bee2ed8f1b 100644
--- a/tools/iio/iio_generic_buffer.c
+++ b/tools/iio/iio_generic_buffer.c
@@ -131,7 +131,8 @@ static void print2byte(uint16_t input, struct iio_channel_info *info)
 		printf("%05f ", ((float)input + info->offset) * info->scale);
 		break;
 	case 'f': {
-#if defined(__FLT16_MAX__)
+#if (!(defined(__x86_64__) || defined(__i386__)) || defined(__SSE2__)) && \
+	defined(__FLT16_MAX__)
 		union {
 			uint16_t u;
 			_Float16 f;
-- 
2.56.0

